      "principle": "The court will not grant divorce on the ground of non-consummation unless it is proved that there was no possibility of consummation.",
      "held": "It is settled law that a court will not grant divorce on the ground of non-consummation unless it is proved that there was no possibility of consummation. The court has consistently taken the view that mere failure to consummate does not entitle a party to a decree of divorce.",
